      "Tech Job Categories": "User Experience, Product Management, Development, Operations, Information Technology",
      "Relationship to Job Industries": "Skills and Job Industries are related in the following ways:\n1. People carry transferable skills with them from one industry into another.\n2. Each industry gives people a starting set of skills shaped by its everyday work.",
      "Read Me File": [
        {
          "name": "skills.md",
          "url": "https://baserow-backend-production20240528124524339000000001.s3.amazonaws.com/user_files/f5GlXHiCQYGNcA6mJJZ7AlSbcsPaDhQX_4b3aba1619f4006f83ffc31bc834f0cf52d63c6242ee8db17dea67db123b8947.md"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spf:job-function",
      "type": [
        "schema:DefinedTermSet",
        "spf:DataType",
        "skos:ConceptScheme"
      ],
      "Data Type Name": "Job Function",
      "Data Type Description": "The label used to describe responsibilities at a company.",
      "Relationship to Skills": "Job Functions and Skills are related in the following ways:\n1. A job function points to the skills a person is expected to have.\n2. People qualify for a job function by having the skills it calls for.",
      "Relationship to Practices": "Job Functions and Practices are related in the following ways:\n1. A job function is done well when a person brings strong team practices to it.\n2. Practices define the human, behavioral side of doing a job function well.",
      "Relationship to Projects": "Job Functions and Projects are related in the following ways:\n1. Job functions bring the different kinds of people a project needs.\n2. Projects bring together people from different job functions.",
      "Relationship to Duties": "Job Functions and Duties are related in the following ways:\n1. A job function is made up of the duties a person is expected to own.\n2. A duty is a set of responsibilities that can sit within one or more job functions.",
      "Relationship to Stakeholders": "Job Functions and Stakeholders are related in the following ways:\n1. Each job function interacts with stakeholders in its own way.\n2. Stakeholders interact with many different job functions on a team.",
      "Relationship to Milestones": "Job Functions and Milestones are related in the following ways:\n1. Different job functions lead at different milestones.\n2. Milestones call on different job functions at different stages.",
      "Relationship to Tools": "Job Functions and Tools are related in the following ways:\n1. Each job function tends to rely on its own set of tools.\n2. The tools a person uses are often tied to their job function.",
      "Relationship to Activities": "Job Functions and Activities are related in the following ways:\n1. A job function is defined by the activities it is responsible for.\n2. Activities are divided among different job functions.",
      "Relationship to Deliverables": "Job Functions and Deliverables are related in the following ways:\n1. Each job function is known for the deliverables it produces.\n2. Different job functions own different deliverables.",
      "Relationship to Job Functions": "Job Functions and other Job Functions are related in the following ways:\n1. Job functions work alongside each other and often overlap on a team.\n2. One job function frequently depends on the work of another.",
      "Relationship to Job Specializations": "Job Functions and Job Specializations are related in the following ways:\n1. A job function can deepen into one or more specializations.\n2. A specialization is a narrower focus that lives inside a broader job function.",
      "Relationship to Company Types": "Job Functions and Company Types are related in the following ways:\n1. A job function adapts its focus to the company type it sits in.\n2. The same job function can look different across company types.",
      "Relationship to Methodologies": "Job Functions and Methodologies are related in the following ways:\n1. Job functions take on specific roles within a methodology.\n2. A methodology assigns specific roles to different job functions.",
      "Relationship to Workshops": "Job Functions and Workshops are related in the following ways:\n1. Different job functions lead or take part in different workshops.\n2. Workshops bring different job functions together to collaborate.",
      "Relationship to Job Industries": "Job Functions and Job Industries are related in the following ways:\n1. Job functions exist across industries, often under different titles.\n2. Industries have their own job functions, often with different titles.",
      "Read Me File": [
        {
          "name": "job-function.md",
          "url": "https://baserow-backend-production20240528124524339000000001.s3.amazonaws.com/user_files/2fRa1iYMalRYy2WVWznLN1g7Rdf8Ooed_6020ccfdb2bd82b7664430bcd3242a9b24bce9ccea5b49642a17272d835e5f64.md"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "spf:job-specialization",
      "type": [
        "schema:DefinedTermSet",
        "spf:DataType",
        "skos:ConceptScheme"
      ],
      "Data Type Name": "Job Specialization",
      "Data Type Description": "An subject matter area of expertise.",
      "Relationship to Skills": "Specializations and Skills are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialization tells you which deeper skills a person has focused on.\n2. A person's cluster of related skills adds up to a specialization.",
      "Relationship to Practices": "Specializations and Practices are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialist still depends on team practices to work well with others.\n2. Practices support any specialization by shaping how a specialist works with the rest of the team.",
      "Relationship to Projects": "Specializations and Projects are related in the following ways:\n1. Specializations bring focused expertise to the parts of a project that need it.\n2. Projects draw on a range of specializations to cover all the work.",
      "Relationship to Duties": "Specializations and Duties are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialization shapes which duties a person is best suited to own.\n2. A duty often calls for a certain specialization to do it well.",
      "Relationship to Stakeholders": "Specializations and Stakeholders are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialization adds depth that helps meet specific stakeholder needs.\n2. Stakeholders benefit from the depth a specialization brings to the work.",
      "Relationship to Milestones": "Specializations and Milestones are related in the following ways:\n1. Certain milestones lean on particular specializations.\n2. Milestones may need certain specializations at particular points in the work.",
      "Relationship to Tools": "Specializations and Tools are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialization often comes with its own specialized tools.\n2. Some tools are specialized, mastered mainly by people in a given specialization.",
      "Relationship to Activities": "Specializations and Activities are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialization focuses a person on a specific set of activities.\n2. Some activities call for a particular specialization.",
      "Relationship to Deliverables": "Specializations and Deliverables are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialization is often recognized by the deliverables it produces.\n2. A specialization is often known for the deliverables it produces.",
      "Relationship to Job Functions": "Specializations and Job Functions are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialization is a deeper focus within a broader job function.\n2. A job function can deepen into one or more specializations.",
      "Relationship to Job Specializations": "Specializations and other Job Specializations are related in the following ways:\n1. Specializations sit near each other, and people often blend two into their own focus.\n2. Growing one specialization can open the door to a related one.",
      "Relationship to Company Types": "Specializations and Company Types are related in the following ways:\n1. Some specializations are more in demand in certain company types.\n2. Some specializations are in higher demand in certain company types.",
      "Relationship to Methodologies": "Specializations and Methodologies are related in the following ways:\n1. A specialization applies its expertise within the team's methodology.\n2. A methodology gives specialists a shared way to work together.",
      "Relationship to Workshops": "Specializations and Workshops are related in the following ways:\n1. Specialists often lead the workshops tied to their area of focus.\n2. Workshops let specialists share their expertise with the team.",
