      ],
      "Data Type Name": "Tool",
      "Data Type Description": "An object (physical or digital) that’s used to complete work.",
      "Relationship to Skills": "Tools and Skills are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools extend a person's skills and usually take skill to operate well.\n2. People rely on their skills to use tools effectively.",
      "Relationship to Practices": "Tools and Practices are related in the following ways:\n1. How openly a team uses its tools reflects its practices.\n2. Practices influence how openly and collaboratively a team uses its tools.",
      "Relationship to Projects": "Tools and Projects are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools support the work of a project and keep the team organized.\n2. Projects rely on a set of tools to get the work done and stay organized.",
      "Relationship to Duties": "Tools and Duties are related in the following ways:\n1. The tools a person reaches for are often set by the duty they hold.\n2. Each duty comes with the tools a person is expected to use.",
      "Relationship to Stakeholders": "Tools and Stakeholders are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools help teams share progress and outputs with stakeholders.\n2. Stakeholders may request certain tools or need access to the team's outputs.",
      "Relationship to Milestones": "Tools and Milestones are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools help teams reach and track their milestones.\n2. Milestones often require specific tools to reach and to show progress.",
      "Relationship to Tools": "Tools and other Tools are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools are often used together, with one tool feeding into another.\n2. Choosing one tool can shape which other tools a team needs.",
      "Relationship to Activities": "Tools and Activities are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools are what people use to carry out many activities.\n2. Activities are carried out using the team's tools.",
      "Relationship to Deliverables": "Tools and Deliverables are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools are used to build and refine deliverables.\n2. Deliverables are created and refined using the team's tools.",
      "Relationship to Job Functions": "Tools and Job Functions are related in the following ways:\n1. The tools a person uses are often tied to their job function.\n2. Each job function tends to rely on its own set of tools.",
      "Relationship to Job Specializations": "Tools and Job Specializations are related in the following ways:\n1. Each specialization leans on its own set of tools to do the work.\n2. Learning a specialization usually means learning the tools that come with it.",
      "Relationship to Company Types": "Tools and Company Types are related in the following ways:\n1. A tool may be standard in one company type and rare in another.\n2. The tools a team uses can depend on the company type.",
      "Relationship to Methodologies": "Tools and Methodologies are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools support the way a methodology asks a team to work.\n2. A methodology guides which tools a team reaches for.",
      "Relationship to Workshops": "Tools and Workshops are related in the following ways:\n1. Tools like shared boards and templates are what make workshops run.\n2. Workshops make use of shared tools like boards and templates.",
