      "Relationship to Practices": "Projects and Practices are related in the following ways:\n1. Projects are where a team's practices get tested under real pressure.\n2. Practices set the tone for how a team works together to deliver a project.",
      "Relationship to Projects": "Projects and other Projects are related in the following ways:\n1. A project can build on the lessons and outputs of earlier projects.\n2. Larger projects are often made up of smaller connected projects.",
      "Relationship to Duties": "Projects and Duties are related in the following ways:\n1. Projects assign duties to people so the work has clear ownership.\n2. Duties give a project clear ownership by setting who is responsible for what.",
      "Relationship to Stakeholders": "Projects and Stakeholders are related in the following ways:\n1. Projects exist to deliver value to their stakeholders.\n2. Stakeholders set the direction and success measures for a project.",
      "Relationship to Milestones": "Projects and Milestones are related in the following ways:\n1. Projects are broken into milestones that mark progress along the way.\n2. Milestones break a project into clear stages of progress.",
      "Relationship to Tools": "Projects and Tools are related in the following ways:\n1. Projects rely on a set of tools to get the work done and stay organized.\n2. Tools support the work of a project and keep the team organized.",
      "Relationship to Activities": "Projects and Activities are related in the following ways:\n1. Projects are made up of many activities the team carries out over time.\n2. Activities are the day-to-day work that moves a project forward.",
      "Relationship to Deliverables": "Projects and Deliverables are related in the following ways:\n1. Projects produce deliverables as the concrete results of the work.\n2. Deliverables are the concrete results a project is judged by.",
      "Relationship to Job Functions": "Projects and Job Functions are related in the following ways:\n1. Projects bring together people from different job functions.\n2. Job functions bring the different kinds of people a project needs.",
