      "Relationship to Skills": "Company Types and Skills are related in the following ways:\n1. Different company types lean on different skills, so the setting shapes which skills matter most.\n2. The skills a person has help them fit the way different company types work.",
      "Relationship to Practices": "Company Types and Practices are related in the following ways:\n1. Every company type benefits from healthy team practices, whatever its structure.\n2. Practices help a team stay healthy no matter which company type they work in.",
      "Relationship to Projects": "Company Types and Projects are related in the following ways:\n1. The company type shapes how a project is scoped and delivered.\n2. Projects look different depending on the company type running them.",
      "Relationship to Duties": "Company Types and Duties are related in the following ways:\n1. A company type shapes what a given duty involves day to day.\n2. How a duty is defined can shift depending on the company type.",
      "Relationship to Stakeholders": "Company Types and Stakeholders are related in the following ways:\n1. The company type determines who the stakeholders are, like clients at an agency.\n2. Who the stakeholders are changes with the company type, such as clients at an agency.",
