      "Relationship to Tools": "Company Types and Tools are related in the following ways:\n1. The tools a team uses can depend on the company type.\n2. A tool may be standard in one company type and rare in another.",
      "Relationship to Activities": "Company Types and Activities are related in the following ways:\n1. The company type influences which activities a team spends time on.\n2. Which activities a team does can vary by company type.",
      "Relationship to Deliverables": "Company Types and Deliverables are related in the following ways:\n1. Some deliverables are specific to a company type, like a pitch deck at a startup.\n2. Some deliverables, like a statement of work, are tied to certain company types.",
      "Relationship to Job Functions": "Company Types and Job Functions are related in the following ways:\n1. The same job function can look different across company types.\n2. A job function adapts its focus to the company type it sits in.",
      "Relationship to Job Specializations": "Company Types and Job Specializations are related in the following ways:\n1. Different company types call for different specializations.\n2. The same specialization can carry more or less weight depending on the company type.",
