      "Data Type Description": "A step-by-step process to carry out work.",
      "Relationship to Skills": "Methodologies and Skills are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology calls for certain skills, like facilitation or planning, to run it well.\n2. People apply their skills within a methodology to guide how the work flows.",
      "Relationship to Practices": "Methodologies and Practices are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology only works when the team lives out the practices behind it.\n2. Practices are the mindset that makes a methodology actually work, not just its steps.",
      "Relationship to Projects": "Methodologies and Projects are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology sets how a team plans and runs a project.\n2. Projects are guided by a methodology that sets how the team works.",
      "Relationship to Duties": "Methodologies and Duties are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology shapes the duties and roles people take on.\n2. Duties are shaped by the methodology the team follows.",
      "Relationship to Stakeholders": "Methodologies and Stakeholders are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology defines how and when stakeholders stay involved.\n2. Stakeholders are kept involved through methodologies that value collaboration.",
      "Relationship to Milestones": "Methodologies and Milestones are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology organizes the work into milestones and cycles.\n2. Milestones are organized by the methodology the team uses to plan work.",
      "Relationship to Tools": "Methodologies and Tools are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology guides which tools a team reaches for.\n2. Tools support the way a methodology asks a team to work.",
      "Relationship to Activities": "Methodologies and Activities are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology sequences the activities a team carries out.\n2. Activities are organized and sequenced by the team's methodology.",
      "Relationship to Deliverables": "Methodologies and Deliverables are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology shapes which deliverables a team creates and when.\n2. Which deliverables a team makes is shaped by its methodology.",
      "Relationship to Job Functions": "Methodologies and Job Functions are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology assigns specific roles to different job functions.\n2. Job functions take on specific roles within a methodology.",
      "Relationship to Job Specializations": "Methodologies and Job Specializations are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology shapes how a specialization does its day-to-day work.\n2. Some specializations lean on certain methodologies more than others.",
      "Relationship to Company Types": "Methodologies and Company Types are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology may fit some company types better than others.\n2. The company type can influence which methodology a team adopts.",
      "Relationship to Methodologies": "Methodologies and other Methodologies are related in the following ways:\n1. Methodologies borrow from one another, and teams often blend them.\n2. A team may switch methodologies as its needs change.",
      "Relationship to Workshops": "Methodologies and Workshops are related in the following ways:\n1. A methodology often comes with workshops that put it into practice.\n2. Workshops put a methodology into practice through guided sessions.",
