      "Data Type Name": "Job Industry",
      "Data Type Description": "A category for companies that perform a certain type of work.",
      "Relationship to Skills": "Job Industries and Skills are related in the following ways:\n1. Each industry gives people a starting set of skills shaped by its everyday work.\n2. People carry transferable skills with them from one industry into another.",
      "Relationship to Practices": "Job Industries and Practices are related in the following ways:\n1. People bring transferable practices, like collaboration, from any industry.\n2. Practices are transferable behaviors people can bring from any industry into tech work.",
      "Relationship to Projects": "Job Industries and Projects are related in the following ways:\n1. The industry shapes what a project is trying to achieve.\n2. Projects can serve any industry, shaping the work to that industry's needs.",
      "Relationship to Duties": "Job Industries and Duties are related in the following ways:\n1. An industry gives a duty its real-world context and expectations.\n2. Duties carry across industries, even when the context changes.",
      "Relationship to Stakeholders": "Job Industries and Stakeholders are related in the following ways:\n1. The industry shapes who the stakeholders are and what they expect.\n2. Stakeholders come from the industry the work is being done for.",
      "Relationship to Milestones": "Job Industries and Milestones are related in the following ways:\n1. Industry norms influence which milestones a project follows.\n2. Milestones adapt to the norms and expectations of the industry.",
      "Relationship to Tools": "Job Industries and Tools are related in the following ways:\n1. Each industry brings its own familiar tools, some of which transfer to tech.\n2. Some tools carry over from other industries, while others are new to tech.",
      "Relationship to Activities": "Job Industries and Activities are related in the following ways:\n1. Everyday activities in an industry give people relevant experience.\n2. Many activities are similar across industries, while some are specific to one.",
      "Relationship to Deliverables": "Job Industries and Deliverables are related in the following ways:\n1. The industry shapes which deliverables carry the most weight.\n2. The deliverables that matter can shift with the industry.",
      "Relationship to Job Functions": "Job Industries and Job Functions are related in the following ways:\n1. Industries have their own job functions, often with different titles.\n2. Job functions exist across industries, often under different titles.",
      "Relationship to Job Specializations": "Job Industries and Job Specializations are related in the following ways:\n1. Industries ask for different specializations depending on the work they do.\n2. A specialization can move across industries, even when the work around it changes.",
      "Relationship to Company Types": "Job Industries and Company Types are related in the following ways:\n1. An industry contains many different company types.\n2. A single company type can exist within many different industries.",
      "Relationship to Methodologies": "Job Industries and Methodologies are related in the following ways:\n1. Some industries adopt certain methodologies more than others.\n2. A methodology can be applied across many industries.",
      "Relationship to Workshops": "Job Industries and Workshops are related in the following ways:\n1. The industry someone comes from shapes what they bring to a workshop.\n2. People bring their industry background into the workshops they join.",
      "Relationship to Job Industries": "Job Industries and other Job Industries are related in the following ways:\n1. People often move between industries, carrying their experience with them.\n2. Industries influence one another as ideas and people move across them.",
      "Read Me File": [
